WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.700
Rome, in the second century.

2
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:06.440
Strange rumours spread about
a group who meet in private.

3
00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:10.260
They are called atheists,
because they refuse the gods.

4
00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:13.590
They are accused of
cannibal feasts and incest.

5
00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:16.100
Being a Christian can bring death.

6
00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:21.560
Then a teacher who still wears his philosopher's
cloak writes to the emperor himself.

7
00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:25.370
So how did a philosopher in
a cloak answer the emperor?

8
00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:28.020
In this mission, you'll
follow Justin's journey,

9
00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:31.050
from teacher to teacher,
then to a school in Rome,

10
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.400
and finally to his trial.

11
00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:36.230
Then you'll sort his
arguments into four kinds:

12
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:40.180
political, moral,
philosophical and theological.

13
00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:44.750
Your mission: find out how this philosopher
in a cloak answered the emperor.
